# General Engineering Rules

- Prefer simple, explicit, maintainable solutions over clever solutions.
- Do not introduce new dependencies unless they are necessary.
- Before adding a dependency, explain why it is needed.
- Do not refactor unrelated code while implementing a feature or fixing a bug.
- Make the smallest reasonable change that satisfies the requirement.
- Follow existing project conventions unless there is a clear architectural reason not to.
- Do not duplicate existing functionality.
- Search the codebase before creating new helpers, utilities, abstractions, or modules.
- Avoid premature abstraction.
- Avoid premature optimization.
- Prefer readable names over short names.
- Avoid magic numbers and unexplained constants.
- Keep functions focused on one responsibility.
- Do not silently change public APIs.